Timestamp,concern_summary,resolution_sop,key_topics,sentiment_transition
2025-12-13 02:35:50,Service Listing Activation and GST Eligibility,"1. Verify caller identity. Ask for caller name and registered company name. Confirm the registered mobile number.
2. Confirm GST ownership. Ask if GST is in the business name or another person's name.
3. Advise eligibility based on GST. If GST is not in your business name, recommend free listing only. If GST is in the same business name, explain paid service eligibility.
4. Ask for missing business details. Collect full address and a nearby landmark.
5. Login and navigation. Open the IndiaMART app. Tap the three horizontal lines on the top-left.
6. Go to Seller Store. Click Seller Store > Manage Product.
7. Update address and service locations. Edit business address and add landmark so buyers can find you.
8. Add or edit services. For each service add a clear photo, title, price, short description, and service location. Remove unrelated products (for example, air cooler) if present.
9. Verify category and nature of business. Ensure service category matches the GST nature of business if you plan to upgrade.
10. Set up PNS numbers. Link up to five alternate contact numbers to the PNS so incoming calls ring on all linked numbers.
11. Confirm listing goes live. Save changes and verify the listing appears correctly in search results.
12. Upsell/Value Add: If GST is in the same business name, offer annual paid services for BuyLeads, priority placement, and an assigned account manager to handle queries and improve lead conversion.","GST, PNS number, Seller Store, Manage Product, IndiaMART App, Free listing, Paid services, BuyLeads, Account Manager, Sunil Kumar Painting Services, Rajnagar extension, DVIP mall, Asian paint, 3D painting, Home painting, Air cooler",From confused/concerned about activation to cooperative and satisfied after guided profile updates.
2025-12-13 02:36:12,Dashboard Metrics: Understanding Buyer Enquiry Columns,"1. Greet the caller and ask for permission to verify the account. 2. Ask for the registered mobile number. 3. Ask for company name and location and confirm them aloud. 4. Confirm account type: free seller or paid seller. 5. If audio is poor, ask the caller to repeat or offer to call back. 6. Instruct the caller to log in. 7. Navigate: Go to Dashboard > Enquiries or Leads. 8. Click any requirement or buyer enquiry to open the detailed view. 9. Point to the columns labeled 'Calls Attempted' and 'Responses' on that enquiry. 10. Explain: 'Calls Attempted' shows the recorded call attempts associated with that enquiry. 11. Explain: 'Responses' shows the number of buyer replies or interactions on that enquiry. 12. Clarify privacy: explain that full buyer contact details are accessible only via paid/premium packages or when the buyer shares contact info. 13. If the caller requests to view a buyer page, offer a guided walkthrough of a public sample requirement. Do not share private buyer contact details. 14. If the caller is evaluating premium options, offer to arrange a sales callback and capture the preferred time. 15. Upsell/Value Add: Summarize benefits of premium leads—direct buyer details, buyleads, and priority visibility—and offer to connect to sales now.","Seller Dashboard, Enquiries / Leads, Calls Attempted, Responses, Buyer Profile, Free Seller, Premium Service, Buy Leads, Sales Callback, Turmeric, Rice, Gurugram",Customer started confused and seeking clarification. Conversation became frustrated due to audio and miscommunication. Call ended unresolved with ask to escalate to sales.
2025-12-13 02:36:34,Service Listing and Lead Acquisition for Manpower Provider,"1. Ask the caller to confirm the registered seller name and business. Ask them to open the IndiaMART app and confirm they are logged in.
2. Instruct the seller to tap the three horizontal lines on the top-left of the app.
3. Tell the seller to tap Seller Tools from the menu.
4. Tell the seller to tap Manage Product to view existing listings.
5. Guide the seller to add or edit products by tapping Add Product or Multiple Add.
6. Instruct the seller to upload 3 to 4 clear photos per product, add a concise description, and set prices. Save each product.
7. Advise the seller to raise the listing score above 80 by completing photos, description, and pricing to improve visibility.
8. If irrelevant inquiries came from a wrong requirement, tell the seller to delete that requirement to stop calls.
9. If they need immediate buyer contacts, show them the Buy Lead option and explain single-lead consumption to connect with buyers.
10. Offer support hours and next steps: tell them to contact support between 8:00 AM and 9:00 PM for help or to send photos via WhatsApp for listing assistance.
11. Upsell: Recommend buying Buy Lead credits for instant leads and suggest improving multiple listings to boost organic inquiries.","Seller Tools, Manage Product, Add Product, Buy Lead, Listing Score, 3-4 Photos, Description and Price, Security manpower, Housekeeping manpower, Manpower service, WhatsApp for photos, Support hours 8:00 AM-9:00 PM",Customer started confused and concerned about unwanted calls. After guidance on app navigation and listing steps they became clarified and reassured.
2025-12-13 02:36:54,Catalog Update: Upload Product Images and Details via Seller Portal,"1. Greet the seller and confirm identity. Ask for the registered mobile number and registered business name. 2. Verify which mobile number is registered on the portal. Clarify if multiple numbers belong to the same seller. 3. Instruct the seller to open seller.indiamart.com. Click Login. Enter the registered mobile number. Complete OTP verification. 4. From the dashboard go to Products > My Products. Locate the specific product entry to update. 5. Click the product to open its edit page. On the right/side panel find Photos & Videos or Media. 6. Click Upload. Add clear images and optional video. Include front view, close-up of bristles/texture, packaging, and a usage/context image. 7. Fill product attributes: product type, bristle type, disposable or reusable, brand, MRP/price, short description, and benefits. 8. Save the changes. Preview the product page to confirm photos and details display correctly. 9. If a sales rep provided an official WhatsApp number, you may send photos there. Note: photos sent to WhatsApp may be attached but you must still update details on the portal. 10. If the product does not appear, clear browser cache or log out and log in again. If issues persist, request a support callback or raise a help ticket. 11. Offer Premium Services as value add: explain lead delivery, priority listing, and TrustSeal verification. Ask if the seller wants a callback for plan details.","Seller Tools, seller.indiamart.com, Product Listing, Photos & Videos, WhatsApp upload, Premium Services, TrustSeal, Leads, Toothbrush, Bamboo toothbrush, Bristle type, MRP / Price",Neutral/uncertain due to registration confusion → Cooperative and receptive to instructions; politely declined premium offer.
2025-12-13 02:39:08,Catalog Update: Change Product Listings to New Product Category,"1. Verify the customer by asking for the registered mobile number. Confirm the displayed name. Confirm company name and whether GST remains the same. 2. Ask whether the customer will use the IndiaMART mobile app or desktop. Offer to guide them to download the app if not installed. 3. Instruct the customer to log in with the registered mobile number. Confirm they see their name at the top. 4. Tell the customer to tap the three-line menu at the top. 5. From the menu, ask them to open Seller Tools. If Seller Tools is not visible, ask them to open Manage Product. 6. Instruct them to go to Manage Product and locate the old product listing. 7. Ask them to tap the product name (e.g., the entry showing the old product). 8. Ask them to tap the three dots next to the product name. Offer the options: Edit or Deactivate. 9. If they want to remove old listings, guide them to select Deactivate and confirm. Offer to deactivate the items remotely if the customer prefers. 10. To add the new product, tell them to tap Add Product. 11. In the Add Product form, instruct them to enter the new product name (e.g., charcoal), price, quantity, description, specifications, and upload images. Remind them to add GST details if applicable. 12. Ask them to review and save the new product. Confirm the product appears in Manage Product. 13. Confirm the customer is satisfied and offer additional help. 14. Upsell/value add: Explain subscription benefits for business promotion and offer to transfer the call to the premium team for more information.","Seller Tools, Manage Product, Add Product, Deactivate, Subscription, GST, Mobile App, Three-line menu, IndiaMART, Jeans, Charcoal",Neutral/confused at start to clarified and satisfied at end
2025-12-13 02:39:29,Catalog Onboarding: Activate Service Listing and Update Profile,"1. Verify identity and account. Confirm caller name, registered mobile, and company name. Ask if GST belongs to the same business.
2. Log in to the IndiaMART application with the registered number.
3. Open the left hamburger menu. Tap Seller Store.
4. Go to Manage Product in Seller Store.
5. Edit company profile. Update full address and add a clear landmark.
6. Check GST status. If GST is in your business name, add the GST number in profile. If GST is under another name, do not add it. Use free listing until you get GST in the same name.
7. Remove irrelevant items. Delete any incorrect product entries (for example, remove unrelated air cooler product).
8. Add service listings. For each service, upload photos, set a price, write a short description, and choose the correct service category (3D painting, wall painting, etc.).
9. Specify service locations and coverage area in each listing.
10. Save and publish the listing. Verify the listing shows live in Manage Product.
11. Test receiving inquiries by checking the contact number on the profile and confirming calls come through.
12. Upsell/Value Add: If GST is in your business name, consider upgrading to the annual paid plan to get BuyLeads, higher listing placement, an account manager, and PNS linking of up to five alternate numbers. Contact sales to upgrade.","Seller Store, Manage Product, IndiaMART application, GST, Free Listing, Paid Annual Plan, BuyLeads, PNS (Primary Number Service), Painting Services, 3D painting, Wall painting, Asian paint, Air cooler",Confused/Unable to start → Reassured by guidance → Cooperative and willing to update listing; open to upgrade
2025-12-13 02:39:51,Catalog Dashboard: Understanding Buyer Metrics and Lead Access,"1. Verify identity and login. Ask for the registered mobile and company name. Request the seller to sign in to IndiaMART and confirm they are on the Seller Dashboard. 2. Navigate to the metrics. Go to Dashboard > My Leads or Buyer Requirements. Open a buyer requirement entry. Locate the columns labelled 'Calls Attempted' and 'Responses'. 3. Explain the core meanings and access rules. Tell the customer: 'Calls Attempted' is the number of call attempts logged for that requirement. 'Responses' is the count of buyers who replied or showed interest. Explain that free sellers see summary metrics and may receive direct incoming inquiries. State that full buyer contact details are available only via Premium Leads or a paid package. Show how to unlock a lead: Click 'View Requirement' > Click 'Unlock Contact' or 'Get Lead' and follow the purchase prompts, or request a sales callback for a demo. 4. Offer value add and next steps. Offer a free listing review and tips to improve visibility. Recommend Premium Leads for unmasked buyer contacts. Offer to schedule a sales-team callback to explain packages and ROI.","Seller Dashboard, Calls Attempted, Responses, Buyer Requirements, My Leads, Premium Leads, Free Seller, Catalog, Turmeric, Rice, Sales Callback, Lead Quality",Customer moved from confused to frustrated. Call ended disconnected and the issue remained unresolved.
2025-12-13 02:40:14,Service Listing Visibility and Lead Acquisition for Seller Catalog,"1. Verification and login. Greet seller. Confirm registered mobile number or company name. Ask the seller to open the IndiaMART app and log in. 2. Navigation to product manager. Tap the three-line menu at top-left. Tap Seller Tools. Tap Manage Product. 3. Locate current entries. Check for any existing service listings under Manpower or Security Manpower. 4. Edit or remove incorrect requirements. If a wrong requirement is posted, open it and delete or edit the entry. 5. Add or update a service listing. Tap Add Product or Multiple Add. Choose Service as the category and the correct subcategory. 6. Complete listing details. Upload 3 to 4 clear photos. Add a concise description. Enter a price or rate. Fill all required attributes. 7. Improve listing score. Ensure photos, price and description are complete. Raise the listing score above 80% to boost visibility. 8. Publish and verify. Save and publish the listing. Re-open Manage Product to confirm the listing is visible. 9. Short-term lead option. Advise using Buy Lead to consume individual leads immediately. 10. Support and follow-up. Offer WhatsApp for photo upload help. Inform seller support hours (8:00 AM to 9:00 PM). 11. Upsell / value add. Recommend purchase of Buy Lead credits or a Listing Boost service for faster enquiries. Offer assistance with professional photos and listing optimization.","Seller Tools, Manage Product, Buy Lead, Listing Score, Photos, Description, Price, Service Listing, Security Manpower, WhatsApp Support, Support Hours",Confused and seeking leads -> Clarified after step-by-step guidance -> Reassured and thankful at end
2025-12-13 02:40:30,Catalog Update: Add Product Photos and Details,"1. Verify customer identity by asking for the registered mobile number and vendor name. 2. Confirm which mobile number is registered on the account before proceeding. 3. Instruct the customer to open seller.indiamart.com and log in using the registered mobile number and OTP. 4. On the dashboard go to Products > My Products. 5. Select the existing product to edit or click Add Product to create a new listing. 6. Click the Photos/Videos or Media section for that product. 7. Upload clear product images and optional video. 8. Fill mandatory product fields like title MRP product type description and benefits. 9. Review the preview then Save and Publish the product. 10. If the customer prefers help ask them to send photos to IndiaMART official WhatsApp. Inform them that photos can be uploaded there but product details must still be filled on seller.indiamart.com. 11. Offer premium services as a value add: explain TrustSeal verification priority listings and lead delivery. Ask if they want a callback to discuss plans.","Seller Tools, Product Listing, Photos/Videos Upload, WhatsApp Upload, MRP, Bristle Type, Disposable Product, TrustSeal, Premium Plan, toothbrush, bamboo toothbrush, Unnati Enterprises, seller.indiamart.com",Confused/Uncertain to Reassured and Cooperative
2025-12-13 03:01:33,Catalog Update: Product Listing Change,"1. Confirm the caller by asking and verifying the registered mobile number. 2. Instruct the user to download and open the IndiaMART app. 3. Log in using the verified mobile number and OTP. 4. Confirm the user sees the greeting with their name at the top. 5. Tap the three-line menu at the top. 6. Tap Seller Tools. 7. Tap Manage Product. 8. Locate the existing product entry in the list. 9. Tap the product name or the three dots beside it. 10. To remove old listings, choose Deactivate from the options and confirm. 11. To update the same listing, tap the product name, edit the name and details, and save. 12. To add the new product, tap Add Product. 13. Enter product name, price, quantity, description, and specifications. 14. Save the new product and confirm it appears in Manage Product. 15. Verify GST details are present for the account. 16. Offer monthly or annual subscription for promotion and premium assistance. 17. If the user agrees, transfer or connect them to the premium team for lead promotion and support.","IndiaMART app, Mobile login, Three-line menu, Seller Tools, Manage Product, Add Product, Deactivate, Edit product name, Price, Quantity, Description, Specifications, GST, Subscription (monthly/annual), Jeans, Charcoal, Wood charcoal",Neutral/uncertain to guided and satisfied
2025-12-13 04:48:27,Lead Purchase vs Seller Listing Mismatch,"1. Verify customer identity. Ask for registered name, company name, and mobile number. Confirm the transaction amount and time. 2. Ask the customer to log in or guide them to log in. Say: Go to Seller Dashboard > Payments > Transactions. 3. In Transactions, locate the ₹470 entry. Click View Details. 4. Check transaction type. If it shows 'Single Lead' or 'Buyer Details', tell the customer this payment bought one buyer lead. 5. Navigate to My Requirements or Enquiries. Click the listed requirement. If the customer did not intend to post a requirement, click Delete or Disable. 6. Navigate to My Catalog > My Listings. Confirm seller listings are active and correct. Turn off any unwanted 'buy' posts. 7. If the customer requests a refund and it meets policy, Click Raise Refund or Contact Billing Team. Note the refund reference ID and share ETA. 8. If the transaction is non-refundable or within policy limits, explain options clearly: use the single lead contact, or request support to escalate. 9. Offer immediate assistance: if the customer wants, arrange a callback from the packages team. Transfer the call or create a callback ticket. 10. Close with value add. Explain package benefits for sellers. Offer a short trial or a package demo to get daily leads.","Seller Tools, Payments, Leads, Single Lead, Requirements, My Catalog, Refund, Packages, Buyer Details, Transactions, silica sand, ₹470, Sai Enterprises",Customer confused and frustrated about payment purpose to calmer and agreeable after explanation and callback arrangement.
2025-12-13 06:14:59,Catalog Update: Product Category Change,"1. Verify the account by confirming the registered mobile number and account name. 2. Open the IndiaMART app or website and log in with the registered mobile number. 3. Tap the menu (three horizontal lines) at the top. 4. Select Seller Tools, then choose Manage Product. 5. Locate the existing product entry shown as the old category. 6. Tap the three dots next to the product name. 7. To remove the old listing, select Deactivate and confirm. 8. To rename instead of deactivating, open the product name, delete the old name, enter the new product name, and save. 9. To add a new product, go to Add Product, enter product name (e.g., wood charcoal), price, quantity, description, and specifications, then Save. 10. Confirm the new product appears in Manage Product. 11. Inform the seller about GST benefits and subscription plans. 12. Offer premium support or transfer to the subscriptions team for help with advertising and lead generation.","product update, catalog, charcoal, jeans, GST, subscription, Seller Tools, Manage Product, Add Product, Deactivate, mobile app, product description",Angry -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:15:28,Account Activation and Service Catalog Update,"1. Verify identity. Ask caller name and confirm the registered company name and phone number. 2. Ask which interface they are using and instruct them to log in to the IndiaMART app. 3. Navigate to Menu > Seller Store > Manage Product. Core action: Edit Profile > Update address and landmark fields, click Save. Remove any irrelevant product entries. 4. Confirm GST status. If GST is not in the business name, advise that paid features require matching GST and recommend free listing until GST is updated. 5. In Manage Product, add each service as a separate listing. For each listing add a clear photo, price, short title, and a concise description. 6. Set correct service categories and service locations for each listing. Specify offerings like wall painting, 3D painting, and brand services (for example Asian paint services). 7. Review the product list and confirm the listing is live. Perform a quick search to verify visibility. 8. Tell the customer the next action: they must add detailed photos, prices, and descriptions for each service. Offer assistance if needed. 9. Upsell/Value Add: Offer paid subscription for priority placement, BuyLeads, dedicated account manager, and PNS multi-number linking to avoid missed calls. Explain that paid services work best when GST matches the business name.","subscription, GST, profile update, free listing, paid services, Seller Store, Manage Product, PNS number, BuyLeads, 3D painting, Asian paint services, air cooler, Rajnagar extension, DVIP mall, Sunil Kumar Painting Services",Neutral -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:15:51,Dashboard: Understanding Buyer Catalog Metrics,"1. Verify identity: ask for the registered mobile number and company name. 2. Remind the user not to share OTPs or passwords. 3. Ask the user to log in to their IndiaMART seller account. 4. Navigate to My IndiaMART > Dashboard > Buyer Catalog or Buyer Requests. 5. Open any buyer inquiry entry to view details. 6. Check the 'Calls attempted' column. It shows the number of contact attempts recorded for that inquiry. 7. Check the 'Responses' column. It shows replies or engagements recorded against that inquiry. 8. Use filters for date, product category, and status to refine counts. 9. Note that full buyer contact details are provided only via Premium Buyleads. 10. If the customer wants buyer contacts or a demo, arrange a sales team callback to explain premium packages and benefits.","dashboard, subscription, buyleads, buyer details, free seller, premium services, inquiries, calls attempted, responses, turmeric, sales callback",Angry -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:16:13,Lead Acquisition for Service Listings,"1. Verify login. Open the IndiaMART app and confirm you are signed in with your seller account. 2. Navigate to seller tools. Tap the three-line menu, then tap Seller Tools, then tap Manage Product. 3. View or add products. In Manage Product tap Add Product or Multiple Add. Upload 3–4 clear photos. Enter a concise description and a price for each product or service. 4. Improve listing score. Check the score shown next to each listing. Complete missing fields and images to raise the score above 80 percent. 5. Use lead options. To connect immediately, go to Buy Leads and consume single leads (paid). Note that subscription plans are not offered for service listings. 6. Support and next steps. If you need help, WhatsApp photos or contact support between 8:00 AM and 9:00 PM. 7. Value add. Consider consuming targeted Buy Leads for faster buyer connections and use high-quality photos and full details to boost organic inquiries.","Seller Tools, Manage Product, Buy Leads, product listing score, security manpower, service listing, IndiaMART app, plans, WhatsApp, support hours",Neutral -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:16:48,Product Listing: Photo Upload and Caller Verification,"1. Verify identity. Ask for the registered mobile number and the caller's name. Confirm the employee who called. 2. Log in to the seller portal. Open seller.indiamart.com. Enter the registered mobile number and complete OTP verification. 3. Navigate to Products. On the left menu click Products. Open your product list. 4. Open the target product. Select the product you want to update. Click the Photo/Video option. 5. Upload media. Upload clear photos and videos of the product. 6. Add product details. Enter type of toothbrush, bristle type, disposable or not, brand, MRP and selling price. Save the changes. 7. Confirm cost. Tell the seller that adding photos and details is free of cost. 8. Alternative via WhatsApp. Inform the seller they can send photos to the official IndiaMART WhatsApp; photos may be added but product details must still be entered on the portal. 9. Upsell and next step. Explain premium benefits like daily leads, priority listing and TrustSeal certification. Offer to schedule a follow-up call or transfer to the premium team.","verification, photos, premium services, toothbrush, bamboo toothbrush, seller.indiamart.com, WhatsApp, TrustSeal, MRP, login, OTP, Unnati Enterprises",Neutral -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:17:07,Catalog Update: Unauthorised Profile and Product Changes,"1. Verify identity. Ask for the registered phone number and confirm the account name. 2. Confirm login on seller.indiamart.com. If logged into buyer.indiamart.com, logout and login at seller.indiamart.com. 3. Open the left hand menu. Click Products. 4. Switch to the Active tab to view live products. 5. Locate the affected product. Click the three-dot action menu next to the product. 6. Click Deactivate to remove the product from public view. 7. Switch to the Inactive tab. Locate the deactivated product. Click the three-dot action menu and select Delete to remove it from the system. 8. To re-add or update photos, use Quick Add at the top or open the product, click Edit, upload new images, and Save. 9. Advise the customer that deletion is permanent. Offer to assist with deletion if needed. 10. Value add: Recommend enabling profile/photo approval or using IndiaMART's Profile Review support to prevent unauthorized updates. Offer help to schedule assisted photo upload.","profile, products, deactivate, delete, photos, seller.indiamart.com, buyer.indiamart.com, Quick Add, Active, Inactive, three-dot menu, Swastik Foods, Nitish",Angry -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:17:32,Catalog & Lead Credit Issue: Payable Leads and Photo Upload Request,"1. Greet the seller and verify Seller Name and Registered Mobile number. 2. Confirm Record ID and GLID before proceeding. 3. Log in to the seller dashboard. 4. Navigate to Dashboard > Leads > Lead Manager. 5. Check lead balance and lead consumption history. 6. Explain that leads show as payable when the allocated balance is exhausted. 7. Inform the seller that leads replenish within 24 working hours and that weekly allocations include daily bonus leads. 8. Navigate to Dashboard > Catalog > Products > Product List. 9. Identify products without images and open each product’s edit page. 10. Ask the seller for product photos. Offer to upload provided images. 11. If seller cannot provide photos, ask for permission to use representative images from Google before uploading. 12. Add or update product images, item names, prices, and item codes in the product edit page. 13. Send the assigned Account Manager contact via SMS and instruct the seller to add a leading zero if required to call. 14. Schedule and confirm an executive callback in one hour for further help. 15. Log the interaction and set follow-up reminders in the CRM. 16. Upsell: Recommend upgrading to the higher or yearly package to get physical meeting support, prioritized assistance, and additional lead services.","leads, lead manager, daily bonus, catalog, product images, account manager, physical meeting, stainless steel pipe, mild steel, Dharmika Iron Store, GLID 52499276, Record ID 674155629",Angry -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:17:52,Account Type Confirmation and Catalog Visibility,"1. Greet the caller and verify the registered name and mobile number. 2. Confirm the account type in the dashboard and state that it is a seller account. 3. Ask and record GST status. 4. Instruct user to open seller.indiamart.com and log in with the registered mobile number. 5. Go to Products > Manage Products in the seller portal. 6. Select the product to edit and click Edit or Update. 7. Upload multiple clear product photos and one product video. 8. Add product attributes, detailed description, and applicable badges. 9. Save changes and publish the product. 10. Check the catalog score and confirm visibility improvements. 11. Recommend value-adds: add GST details when available and offer paid promotions or catalog optimization services to boost visibility.","account type, seller, catalog score, product photos, product videos, GST, seller.indiamart.com, Sarvadhanya Traders, badges, visibility",Neutral -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:18:14,Listing Sales: Skip Subscription to Sell for Free,"1. Verify the caller. Ask for registered mobile number and seller name. Confirm account details. 2. Log in to the IndiaMART seller account. Use the registered mobile or email. 3. Navigate to the seller dashboard. Go to Dashboard > Seller Tools (top-right). 4. Locate the subscription prompt in Seller Tools. Click Skip or Decline the subscription plan. 5. Confirm the product listing status. Ensure 'Receive Inquiries' or listing visibility is enabled so buyers can contact you. 6. If GST or paid-plan information appears, inform the seller that GST entry is for paid subscriptions only and is optional for free listings. 7. Upsell: Offer BuyLeads or a paid subscription for priority visibility and faster inquiries. Offer assistance to activate the paid plan if the seller wants it.","subscription, Seller Tools, BuyLeads, Free Listing, GST, Sketchup Store",Neutral -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:18:38,Catalog Update: Unauthorized Modifications,"1. Greet and verify the caller. Confirm name, company, registered phone, Record ID, and GLID. 2. Log into the agent console. Use your agent credentials. 3. Go to Seller Tools > Catalog Manager. Open Record ID 674231372. 4. Open the product list and click Edit History or Activity Log. 5. Filter changes by date and agent. Look for edits by Akash Sisodia. 6. If a previous version is available, select it and click Restore. Confirm the restore. 7. If restore is not available, create a rollback ticket. Mark reason as ""Unauthorized catalog changes."" Attach screenshots and the call recording link. Set priority to high. 8. Notify Catalog Ops and assign the ticket. Request customer contact on next working day (Monday). Add the appointment in CRM. 9. Inform the customer on call. Give the ticket ID, explain the action taken, and confirm the Monday callback time. 10. Log full details in CRM. Include notes, timestamp, audio link, Record ID, and GLID. 11. Offer a value add. Propose catalog protection, scheduled catalog audits, or a dedicated account manager for prevention.","catalog, prices, pictures, appointment, rollback, Edit History, Seller Tools, Catalog Ops, Om Enterprises, Akash Sisodia, Record ID 674231372, GLID 160733333",Angry -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:19:07,Catalog Update: Location Preference and Category Addition Request,"1. Greet the caller and verify identity. Confirm caller name, company name, registered email or phone, GLID and Record ID. 2. Confirm the exact issue. Ask whether the problem is location preference, buyleads visibility, or missing product categories. 3. Ask the caller to open their IndiaMART dashboard. Direct them: Profile > Buyleads > Filters > Location. 4. Explain the location preference behavior. State that preferred locations are auto-set based on buylead consumption and cannot be manually edited. 5. Show the filter workaround. In Filters > Location select 'Uttar Pradesh' and Apply to view leads across UP immediately. 6. Explain major-city mapping. Tell the caller that major cities appear based on lead consumption; advise consistent lead response to influence preferred cities over time. 7. For adding categories, offer a live assist. Share a video-meet link to the caller's registered email and schedule/join the meet to map and add categories together. 8. During the meeting navigate: Profile > Products/Categories > Add Category. Add each requested category, save changes, and confirm visible listing with the customer. 9. If you lack permission to add categories, create a category-add ticket. Include caller name, company, GLID, list of categories, and urgency. Send confirmation of the ticket to the registered email. 10. If the customer reports an unhelpful account manager, escalate internally. Create an Account Management ticket and flag for follow-up by the assigned AM. 11. Close the call by summarizing actions taken and next steps. Confirm the meeting time or ticket number. 12. Upsell/value add: Offer a category audit or Premium Listing assistance and a dedicated account manager for faster category on-boarding.","location preference, buyleads, categories, account manager, Uttar Pradesh, major cities, filters, video meet, Solar panels, Solar water pump, Bharat Solar Green Energy, GLID 243133193, Record ID 674227532",Angry -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:19:23,Catalog Management: Add / Edit / Delete Product,"1. Verify caller identity. Ask for Seller ID and GLID. Confirm Record ID 674251313. 2. Confirm account access. Ask if seller can log into dashboard now. 3. Instruct to open seller dashboard. Go to Seller Tools. 4. Navigate to Catalog Manager. Click My Products or Product Listing. 5. To add a product: Click Add Product. Enter title, category, price, SKU, GST details, and upload images. Click Save as Draft. Then click Publish. 6. To edit a product: Use Search or filter. Enter GLID 255942960 or Record ID. Click Edit. Update required fields. Click Save. Then click Publish. 7. To delete or deactivate a product: Search by GLID or Record ID. Select the product. Click Delete or Deactivate. Confirm the action. 8. Verify change. Refresh the product list. Confirm status shows Active, Draft, or Deleted. 9. Log the change. Note GLID, Record ID, action taken, and timestamp. 10. Ask if they need a bulk action. Offer to send CSV template. 11. Offer value add. Suggest premium listing, catalog optimization, or dedicated support.","Catalog Management, Product Add, Product Edit, Product Delete, Seller Tools, Catalog Manager, Product Listing, Bulk Upload, GST, GLID 255942960, Record 674251313",No audio available; sentiment unknown.
2025-12-13 06:19:45,Catalog Update: Price Adjustments for Listings,"1. Greet the seller and verify identity. Ask for company name and registered mobile or email. Confirm Record ID 674274194 or GLID 256517489. 2. Confirm access method. Ask if seller can use the Seller App or needs you to update from the portal. 3. Log in to the Seller Dashboard. Or open Seller App. Use verified credentials. 4. Navigate to Products. Click My Listings or Menu > My Products. 5. Search for the specific product names. Select Garlic paste, Onion paste, and Ginger paste listings. Click Edit on each listing. 6. Update the price fields. Set Garlic paste to ₹440 per kg. Set Onion paste to ₹200. Confirm Ginger paste price with the seller before changing. 7. Click Save or Update. Publish the listing and wait for confirmation. 8. Verify the live listing. Open each product page. Confirm the updated price displays correctly. 9. Notify the seller. Send confirmation via SMS or email. Note the updated prices and any pending items. 10. Upsell and value add. Recommend uploading clear product images, detailed descriptions, GST info, and delivery terms. Offer to assist with image uploads and listing optimization.","Price Change, Product Details, Seller Dashboard, Seller App, Garlic Paste, Onion Paste, Ginger Paste, GST, Images",Angry -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:20:08,Catalog Assistance: Add or Modify Product Listings,"1. Greet the seller and ask for the registered mobile number and company name. 2. Verify the seller by matching the number and company with the Record ID or GLID. 3. Log in to the Seller Dashboard with your agent credentials. 4. Go to Catalog > Products > My Products. 5. Search the account by registered number or GLID and open the product list. 6. For add/edit requests, click Add Product or Edit next to the target listing and update fields as required. 7. If the assigned field executive is not reachable, create an escalation ticket. Mark it as 'Field Visit Requested' and set urgent priority if the seller requests a visit. 8. Send the account manager contact to the seller via SMS and email. Read the helpline number aloud and confirm the seller has noted it. 9. Offer to schedule a field visit and confirm tentative date and time with the seller. 10. Close the call by offering value add: propose a paid on-site assistance or catalog optimisation service to highlight listings.","products, catalog update, escalation, helpline, account manager, Anand Fitness, Manish Kumar, field visit, Record ID 674279450, GLID 88479326, registered number 98279827833, helpline 97027072707",Angry -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:20:45,Catalog Issue: Bulk Excel Upload and Location-based Lead Targeting,"1. Verify identity. Confirm buyer name, company, and registered mobile or email. Ask customer to stay on call. 2. Ask customer to log in to the Seller Dashboard. Confirm they are on the BuyLeads page. 3. Navigate to BuyLeads > Click Filters. Open the Location filter. 4. Drag or expand the location list. Click Search city or state. Type the desired location name, for example Phulgaon MIDC. 5. Apply the location filter. If needed, enable the Nearby option to widen radius. Confirm filtered leads are displayed. 6. Confirm whether products are visible in the catalog. If products are missing, proceed to raise a support ticket. 7. Raise a ticket: Go to Support/Help > Raise Complaint > Category: Catalog Upload. Attach the excel or note the sheet details. Mention approximate product count (e.g., 200). Submit the ticket and record the ticket ID. 8. Escalate the ticket to the concerned team for manual verification and upload. Request a callback from the operations team and note expected SLAs. 9. Offer immediate assistance: Propose a video meet. Send a calendar invite to the registered email. Use the session to walk through filters and verify uploads. 10. Upsell / Value add: Offer profile optimization or Paid Lead Targeting services to increase lead flow. Propose a short onboarding session for faster results.","buyleads, location filter, excel sheet, products, Phulgaon MIDC, Pune, ticket escalation, video meet, profile optimization, Paid Lead Targeting",Angry -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:21:03,Catalog Update: Add Product to Seller Catalog,"1. Verify the seller. Ask for name and registered mobile number. Confirm they are logged into the IndiaMART account. 2. Ask the seller to open the IndiaMART mobile app. Instruct them to login if needed. 3. Direct them to Seller Tools. 4. Tap Manage Products. 5. Look for the plus icon or 'Add Product' / 'Add More' prompt at the bottom. 6. Tap Add Product. 7. Enter product name, select the correct category and unit (litre, kg etc.). 8. Add price and any variant or quantity details. 9. Upload clear product photos. 10. Save and publish the product to the catalog. 11. If Add Product is not visible, ask them to update the app, clear cache, or check category filters. 12. If they cannot upload photos, request images via WhatsApp for manual update by the support team. 13. Offer value add: Recommend enriching the listing with high-quality photos and complete specifications. Offer premium listing or seller tools to boost visibility.","add product, seller tool, catalog, mobile app, manage product, price, photos, WhatsApp, support team, ghee, butter, ice cream",Neutral -> Positive
2025-12-13 06:21:24,Catalog Optimization: Low Visibility and Inquiries,"1. Ask the seller to log in. Confirm the registered mobile or email. Open seller.indiamart.com on desktop or the IndiaMART Seller app on mobile. 2. From the dashboard go to Products. Click My Products or Products on the left menu. Select the listed item and click Edit. Then go to Profile > Company Details. 3. Update product information. Upload at least 3 clear photos. Enter accurate price, choose the exact category, and add detailed specifications. Write a full product description and add keywords or tags. Save and publish. 4. Update company profile fields. Set business type as Retailer. Enter complete address and contact details. Add GST number and upload GST proof when available. Save changes. 5. Check the Catalog Score on the product page. Follow the platform checklist to fix missing fields until the score improves. 6. Advise the seller to refresh and monitor listings regularly. Encourage timely replies to inquiries. 7. Value add: Inform the seller that adding GST enables Premium eligibility. Recommend upgrading to Premium after GST verification to increase visibility and lead flow.","catalog score, product details, GST, premium, watches, seller.indiamart.com, IndiaMART Seller app",Neutral -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:21:56,Catalog Visibility: Product Not Visible to Buyers,"1. Greet and verify the caller by confirming registered company name, registered email, and phone number. 2. Ask the seller to log in to the Seller Dashboard. 3. Go to Catalog > My Products > All Listings. 4. Search the product by name or GLID. 5. Open the product listing and check the listing status field. 6. If the status is Draft or Inactive, click Edit, change status to Live or Publish, and click Save. 7. If the status is Live but still not visible, check Visibility settings and category approval notes. Toggle Visibility to Public and save. 8. Ask the seller to open an incognito browser or clear cache and check public view. 9. If the issue persists, offer a screen-share via video meet. Send the meet link to the registered email or to the seller's WhatsApp after they send a 'Hi'. 10. Join the video meet, share screen, reproduce the issue, and make required edits or publish the listing from the agent side if allowed. 11. Confirm visibility by checking the public listing and ask the customer to verify. 12. Offer product listing optimization tips and a paid boost/promotion as a value-add.","product visibility, video meet, email id, Seller Dashboard, Catalog, My Products, Publish, Draft, Visibility Settings, Screen Share, WhatsApp, Arch UVC arch windows, Neomi Print, 571@gmail.com, Mohammad Shafiullah, GLID 222652458",Annoyed -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:22:17,Product Listing: How to Add Products to Seller Account,"1. Verify your account. Confirm the registered mobile number. Log in at seller.indiamart.com or open the IndiaMART B2B Marketplace app. 2. Complete login using the OTP. 3. On the left menu click Product. 4. Choose Add Product or Quick Add. 5. Add a minimum of 3 to 4 products. You may add up to 400 products. 6. For each product upload 3 to 4 clear photos. 7. Enter product title, short description, and price. 8. Add GST and company details if applicable. 9. Click Save and then Save & Continue for each listing. 10. Verify listings in Dashboard or Product List. 11. If you need help, request a callback for hands-on account setup. Explore paid services for premium account design and lead packages.","product, listing, add product, quick add, seller.indiamart.com, IndiaMART B2B Marketplace, photos, minimum 3-4, maximum 400, GST verified, woven fabric, pipe, birthday cap, birthday candle, paid service, lead manager",Angry -> Satisfied
2025-12-13 06:22:41,Catalog Update: Extract Images from Videos,"1. Greet the caller and verify identity. Ask for registered mobile and seller ID.
2. Log in to the Seller Dashboard with your agent credentials.
3. Go to Catalog > Manage Products. Search the product by name or ID. Click Edit.
4. Tell the customer that IndiaMART does not accept video uploads.
5. Request the WhatsApp video link or ask the customer to re-send the video file.
6. Open the video on a desktop or laptop. Play and pause at the desired frame.
7. Take a high-resolution screenshot while the video is paused.
8. Crop and resize the screenshot to recommended dimensions (example: 800x800 px). Save as JPEG or PNG.
9. In Edit Product > Images, click Upload. Select the saved screenshot. Set image order and mark as primary if needed.
10. Click Save or Update product. Wait for confirmation that changes are applied.
11. Share the updated product URL with the customer and confirm satisfaction.
12. Offer a value add: propose image optimization, designer connect, or premium listing to improve visibility.","catalog, video, upload, screenshot, WhatsApp, IndiaMART, Sakshi madam, Seller Dashboard, Product Images",Neutral -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:23:01,Account Suspension: Subscription Renewal,"1. Greet the caller and verify identity. Ask for registered mobile, customer name, company name, Record ID, and GLID. 2. Log in to the IndiaMART agent portal. Use your agent ID and password. Open the Seller Console. 3. Navigate to the account area. Go to Seller Console > Account Settings > Subscriptions or Billing > Suspended Accounts. 4. Check suspension details. Note suspension reason, outstanding invoice amount, plan ID, Record ID, and GLID. 5. Inform the customer of dues and renewal options. State the amount and available plans. 6. Obtain payment consent. Offer payment by saved method or send a secure payment link via SMS/email. 7. Process or confirm payment. Verify transaction ID or payment gateway confirmation. 8. Reactivate the account. Click Renew or Reactivate. Update account status to Active. 9. Confirm reactivation to the customer. Share confirmation ID and expected restoration time. 10. Offer post-activation help. Offer to review listings and restore visibility if needed. 11. Upsell/value add. Propose an upgraded subscription or visibility package and explain benefits briefly.","subscription, renewal, account suspension, AJ Battery, Sadiq Mohammad, 9110269256, Record ID 674347337, GLID 75590317, Seller Tools, Billing",Neutral -> Neutral
2025-12-13 06:23:23,Seller Onboarding: Add Products and Contact Support,"1. Verify account. Confirm registered company name and primary mobile number. Ask for GST or registration number if needed.
