2025-12-13 14:15:46,Catalog: Secondary Category and Attributes Auto-Removed,"1. Verify the seller’s identity and confirm login to the Seller Panel. 2. Open the product list on the panel. 3. Select an affected product and click Edit. 4. Open the Categories section. 5. Set the correct Primary and Secondary category. 6. Open the Attributes or Keywords section. 7. Refill fields like material, fabric, thread count, and size. 8. Save and publish the product. 9. Repeat for a few items to confirm the updates are stable. 10. If categories or attributes remove again, contact Support from the panel or helpline and report a recurring technical issue. 11. Share product links and screenshots to help the team replicate the problem, and request a callback within four working hours. 12. For better lead visibility, keep all attributes complete across products and consider upgrading your plan for added visibility.",,Frustrated → Calm
2025-12-13 14:15:46,Support: Reopen and Escalate Unresolved Complaint,"1. Verify the seller’s identity and confirm login to the Seller Panel. 2. Go to the support or complaints section on the panel, or call the helpline. 3. Provide the existing complaint number and state that the issue persists. 4. Ask to reopen or escalate the ticket to the technical team. 5. Add product links and screenshots showing missing secondary category and removed keywords. 6. Request a callback within four working hours and note the new update or reference number. 7. Share or request account manager details for direct coordination. 8. Monitor updates and confirm resolution before closing the ticket. 9. For added value, schedule a quick catalog health review and consider an upgraded plan for higher visibility and faster assistance.",,Frustrated → Calm
2025-12-13 14:23:13,Catalog Attributes and Secondary Category Auto-Removal,"1. Verify the seller’s identity and confirm account login. 2. Ask the seller to open the IndiaMART Seller Panel. 3. Go to the product listings and open the affected product in Edit. 4. Check primary and secondary category. 5. If secondary is missing, re-select the correct secondary category. 6. Review attributes like material, fabric, thread count, size, and keywords. 7. Re-enter any missing fields and save the product. 8. If the fields remove again, create a complaint and share the complaint number. 9. Arrange a callback from the concerned team within four working hours. 10. Value-add: Recommend keeping attributes complete and keyword-rich to improve lead quality and visibility.",,Frustrated → Calm
2025-12-13 14:23:13,Support Escalation for Unresolved Complaint,"1. Verify the seller’s identity and confirm the registered business. 2. Confirm the registered contact number on the account. 3. Check prior complaints for the same issue. 4. If unresolved, register a new complaint referencing the recurring issue. 5. Share the complaint number with the seller. 6. Arrange a callback from the concerned team within four working hours. 7. Share the Account Manager’s contact for direct follow-up. 8. Value-add: Suggest reviewing and updating product attributes meanwhile to maintain lead quality.",,Frustrated → Calm
2025-12-13 14:37:27,Catalog Update: Remove Unwanted Categories to Improve Lead Relevance,"1. Verify the seller identity and confirm account access. 2. Log in to the seller account. 3. Go to the Catalog section. 4. Review all active categories and products. 5. Remove or deactivate categories that do not match the business focus. 6. Delete or unlist unrelated products from those categories. 7. Keep only the relevant categories and products for the business. 8. Save the catalog updates and confirm the changes. 9. Ask the seller to monitor new leads after the update. 10. For higher visibility and better lead quality, offer catalog optimization or a suitable plan upgrade.",,Concerned → Reassured
2025-12-13 14:55:50,Catalog Update: Product Addition and Images Not Updated,"1. Verify the seller identity and log in to the account. 2. Open the product management section. 3. Select Add Product for new items, or Edit for existing listings. 4. Enter all required product details clearly. 5. Upload clear product photos in the required format. 6. Save and publish the product. 7. Recheck the listing to confirm photos and details are visible. 8. If updates do not reflect, raise a support ticket and attach screenshots. 9. For better visibility when you renew, consider Maximizer or a higher plan.","['Add Product', 'Product Photos', 'Scoring', 'Seller Panel', 'Maximizer', 'RK Pharma Kitchen Equipments']",Frustrated → Calm
2025-12-13 14:55:50,Service Complaint: Field Representative Misconduct and Early Renewal Pressure,"1. Verify the seller identity and log in to the account. 2. Go to the Help and Support section. 3. Create a new complaint ticket. 4. Choose the issue type as Service behavior and Product not added. 5. Describe the incident with date, visit details, and what was not done. 6. Attach screenshots of messages as evidence. 7. Submit the ticket and note the complaint number. 8. Ask for a callback and escalation to the concerned team. 9. Enable WhatsApp or SMS alerts for faster ticket updates.","['Complaint Ticket', 'Field Executive', 'Misbehavior', 'Early Renewal', 'Screenshot', 'customercare@indiamart.com', 'Complaint number 9723743']",Angry → Neutral
2025-12-13 14:55:50,Account Contact Number Not Recognized,"1. Verify the seller identity and log in to the account. 2. Open Account Settings and then Contact Details. 3. Check the primary and secondary mobile numbers. 4. Add or correct the mobile number that is not showing. 5. Set the preferred number as primary. 6. Save changes and test by requesting a verification or support call. 7. If update is blocked, raise a ticket asking support to update the number. 8. Add an alternate number to avoid missed contact. 9. Enable WhatsApp alerts for quicker communication.","['Registered Mobile Number', 'Secondary Number', 'Contact Details', 'Unable to call support']",Confused → Satisfied
2025-12-13 14:55:50,Lead Flow: Inquiries Not Received Properly,"1. Verify the seller identity and log in to the account. 2. Open the Leads or Enquiries section. 3. Check date filters and lead status to ensure nothing is hidden. 4. Confirm that key products are active and visible. 5. Ensure product details and photos are complete to improve visibility. 6. Review serviceable locations and categories and adjust if needed. 7. Turn on lead alerts via SMS, email, or WhatsApp. 8. If lead flow remains low, raise a support ticket with examples. 9. At renewal, consider Maximizer for higher visibility.","['Leads/Enquiries', 'Lead Flow', 'Product Visibility', 'Product Photos', 'Maximizer']",Frustrated → Calm
2025-12-13 14:59:20,Account Mode Mix-up: Posted Requirement Causing Buyer-Intent Calls,"1. Verify the seller identity and login with the registered mobile or email. 2. Open the Seller Panel dashboard. 3. Go to Requirements or Buy Leads. 4. Check if any requirement is posted as a buyer. 5. Close or delete the posted requirement to stop purchase-intent calls. 6. Go to Catalog or Manage Products. 7. Upload products and complete all listing details. 8. Ensure enquiry preferences are enabled for selling. 9. For higher visibility and steady enquiries, consider a package upgrade.","['Posted Requirement', 'Buy Leads', 'Seller Panel', 'Catalog Upload', 'Manage Products', 'Enquiry Preferences']",Frustrated → Neutral
2025-12-13 14:59:20,Single Lead Payment Clarification,"1. Verify login with the registered credentials. 2. Open the Seller Panel. 3. Go to Payments or Buy Leads. 4. Confirm the 470 transaction against a single lead. 5. Open that lead to view buyer contact details. 6. Call the buyer and pitch your offering. 7. Note the outcome for follow-up. 8. For lower cost per lead and more volume, consider a package.","['470 payment', 'Single Lead', 'Buyer Details', 'Buy Leads', 'Payments', 'Lead Follow-up']",Confused → Neutral
2025-12-13 14:59:20,Package Benefits and Upgrade Guidance,1. Verify the seller account and login. 2. Open the Seller Panel. 3. Go to Upgrade or Packages. 4. Review available packages and listed benefits. 5. Explain that packages provide multiple buyer contacts on a regular (daily or weekly) basis. 6. Compare with a single lead purchase and clarify value. 7. Confirm the preferred package and assist with checkout. 8. Highlight that packages improve visibility and lead volume for faster sales.,"['Packages', 'Upgrade Plan', 'Lead Frequency', 'Buyer Details', 'Single Lead vs Package']",Inquisitive → Neutral
2025-12-13 19:10:52,Lead Generation: No Inquiries Received,"1. Verify the seller using the registered mobile number and email ID. 2. Check the subscription status and last inquiry date in the internal system. 3. Acknowledge the no-call period and validate any reported dates. 4. Review catalog health; if the score is low, inform the seller that missing images reduce visibility. 5. Ask the seller to share at least three product photos via the registered WhatsApp number; note that pricing can be skipped if they cannot disclose it. 6. Raise a concern ticket for low inquiries and inform the expected callback timeline if the team is off, for example by Monday. 7. After updates reflect, review inquiry flow and, if results improve, suggest plan upgrades for higher visibility.","['Lead Volume', 'No calls since August', 'TrustSeal', 'Star subscription', 'Catalog score 33%', 'Raise concern ticket', 'Team off; Monday callback', 'WhatsApp image submission']",Frustrated → Calm
2025-12-13 19:10:52,Catalog Optimization: Low Catalog Score Due to Missing Images,"1. Verify the seller using the registered mobile number and email ID. 2. Check the current catalog score in the internal system. 3. If images are missing, inform the seller that a minimum of three product photos are required; up to ten to twelve can be added. 4. Request the seller to share images from the registered mobile via WhatsApp for faster addition. 5. Submit the images for upload and confirm once they reflect in the catalog. 6. If issues persist despite images, raise a concern ticket for further assistance. 7. After the catalog score improves, recommend visibility boosters or plan upgrades to attract more inquiries.","['Catalog Score', 'Catalog score 33%', 'Product Images', 'Minimum three photos', 'WhatsApp image submission', 'Description and specifications', 'Price optional']",Confused → Cooperative
2025-12-13 19:21:03,Lead Generation: Low and Irrelevant Leads,"1. Verify the registered mobile number and firm name. Log in to the Seller Panel or IndiaMART Seller App. 2. Go to Leads > Buy Leads. Check current availability in your active categories and locations. 3. Go to Leads > Lead Manager. Review the last 30 days of leads. Mark irrelevant leads to train relevance. 4. Go to Catalog > Manage Services/Categories. Add all relevant subcategories under your service domain. Save changes. 5. Go to Profile > Service Locations. Confirm coverage matches your business scope (for example, all India). Save. 6. Go to My Account > Plan Details. Confirm the premium plan is active. 7. Go to Notifications/Alerts. Turn on SMS, email, and app lead alerts. 8. If Buy Leads show low or zero availability, go to Help > Raise a Ticket > Low/Irrelevant Leads. Attach examples and submit. 9. Request a priority callback from the premium desk or the account manager. Share preferred time slots. Note the case ID. 10. For more visibility and better relevance, offer a quick catalog and category audit and guide on keywords to improve lead quality.","['Lead Quality', 'Buy Leads', 'Lead Manager', 'Premium Supplier', 'Category Mapping', 'IndiaMART Seller App', 'Trademark registration services', 'Trademark law attorney', 'Copyright services', 'Intellectual property management', 'Trademark litigation', 'All India service']",Concerned → Neutral
2025-12-13 19:21:03,Account Manager Unreachable,"1. Verify the registered mobile number and firm name. Log in to IndiaMART systems. 2. Open internal CRM. Retrieve the assigned account manager’s name, number, and email. 3. Trigger a priority callback from the account manager. Set the preferred callback window and mark urgency. 4. Share the manager’s contact details and the ticket ID via SMS and email to the registered contacts. 5. Offer alternate premium support options, such as the premium desk and in‑app support. Attempt a live transfer if available. 6. If no response within the agreed window, escalate to the premium support queue. Add notes on missed calls and business impact. 7. As a value add, offer to schedule a performance review call to optimize categories and improve lead flow.","['Account Manager', 'Premium Desk', 'Callback Escalation', 'Ticket ID', 'IndiaMART Seller App', 'Lead Issue']",Frustrated → Neutral
